Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Circle resources read right before the seal

Approving an investigator sent no circle update and filled nothing, so with
four approved the Lightkeeper's open Circle page read each resource as "1 of
1" and "refills to 1 (1 plus the circle's members)", and after a reload as
"1 of 5" with four squares that looked spent. An approval or a rejoin now
sends the campaign's circle to every desk, and before the seal fills each
resource to 1 plus the members first, as the seal does (rulebook p. 41).
After the seal only the maximum grows. The note under the resources puts the
rule before the number: "each refills to 1 plus the circle's members (now 5)".

Tests: the approve and rejoin broadcasts carry the circle, and a new test
approves three before the seal and one after. Checked in Chromium: four
approvals with the Lightkeeper's desk open read 5 of 5, and the same after a
reload.

